Tests for the C++11 library (doc/stdcxx-cxx11.md, doc/stdcxx-cxx11-TODO.md)

  fetch-libcxx.sh DIR    downloads libc++ 8.0.1; its tests are the check
  lcxx.py PATH...        runs libc++ tests with pathCC -fpsclang
                         (--host: with the host clang++ instead)
  hostcc.sh ...          host clang++ with the suite's stdcxx and runtime

  export LIBCXX_SRC=DIR PATH64_STAGE=BUILD/Xcompiler
  ./lcxx.py -v utilities/tuple

Original regression tests can be passed by absolute path:
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/compiler-lifetime.pass.cpp" "$PWD/compiler-virtual-base.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/vector-exceptions.pass.cpp" "$PWD/vector-bool.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/deque-exceptions.pass.cpp" "$PWD/compiler-return-object.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/compiler-unwind.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py -std c++14 "$PWD/sized-delete.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/phase3-algorithms.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/phase3-move-iterators.pass.cpp" "$PWD/compiler-short-circuit.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/move-sorting.pass.cpp" "$PWD/partition-exceptions.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/compiler-member-return.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py "$PWD/compiler-member-init-unwind.pass.cpp" "$PWD/compiler-constructor-cleanup.pass.cpp"
  ./lcxx.py language.support/support.dynamic/alloc.errors "$PWD/new-handler.pass.cpp"

Use --timeout 180 for the deque range-insertion stress test at -O0. The
runner's default per-test runtime limit remains 30 seconds.

The libc++ vector tests erase_iter, erase_iter_iter and vector.special/swap
assume class iterators. With stdcxx's raw pointers, temporary test copies need
qualified std::distance and std::next, and std::prev(v.end()) in place of
--v.end(). Keep the reference sources unchanged and report their compile
failures separately from these adapted checks.

phase3-algorithms.pass.cpp checks min/max tie selection, the minmax_element
comparison bound on exhaustive small sequences through forward iterators,
negative copy counts, numeric generation, bounded comparisons, and C++14
constant evaluation. It needs no <random> implementation.

phase3-move-iterators.pass.cpp checks all insertion adapters with move-only
deque elements and the rotated sequence/return iterator. The reference front
insertion test uses list, whose move insertion is a separate container TODO.
compiler-short-circuit.pass.cpp checks conditional reference materialization,
null pointers, nested operands, exceptions and class temporary destruction.

move-sorting.pass.cpp checks move-only sort, heap and partial-sort contracts,
identity preservation, comparison bounds and packed-bit proxy iterators.
partition-exceptions.pass.cpp substitutes the raw temporary-buffer provider to
check full, partial and failed allocations, stable order and resource cleanup
when moves or predicates throw. It exercises the public stable_partition API.
compiler-member-return.pass.cpp checks calls returning trivial classes into
members at different offsets, and side effects in scalar/trivial destruction.

compiler-member-init-unwind.pass.cpp is the formerly failing aggregate-member
initializer unwind repro. compiler-constructor-cleanup.pass.cpp adds destruction
order, references, base/delegating construction, inner catches and temporary
argument checks. new-handler.pass.cpp checks synchronized get/set operations,
callback reentrancy, throwing/nothrow allocation failure and the new error type.

compiler-array-length.todo.cpp records the remaining negative array-bound
exception-selection issue. It stays outside the .pass.cpp regression set;
both current compiler paths over this runtime reach bad_alloc.
